# warble local-process configuration (sourced by bin/warble).
#
# Copy to warble.env and edit. Used only by the bare-metal/dev path (bin/warble).
# The Docker path (docker-compose.yml) configures services through compose env
# instead and does not read this file.
#
# All values shown are the defaults; uncomment to override.

## Bind host for the local sidecars. The Go server binds 0.0.0.0 regardless
## (the device connects to it over the LAN); these are the loopback sidecars.
# BIND_HOST=127.0.0.1

## Service ports.
# WHISPER_PORT=8082
# PIPER_PORT=8001
# VAD_PORT=8005
# SERVER_PORT=8000
# OLLAMA_PORT=11434

## whisper.cpp server binary. Bare name = found on PATH; or give an absolute path.
# WHISPER_SERVER_BIN=whisper-server
## Whisper model file (relative to the warble root or absolute).
## Default is the small multilingual "base" model. For best accuracy (and the
## heaviest), use ggml-large-v3.bin. Fetch with scripts/fetch-models.sh.
# WHISPER_MODEL=models/whisper/ggml-base.bin
## Transcription language: a 2-letter code (en, ro, de, ...) or "auto" to detect.
# WHISPER_LANG=auto
## Extra decode flags passed verbatim to whisper-server.
# WHISPER_EXTRA_ARGS=-bs 5 -bo 5

## uvicorn launchers for the Python shims. Default to the project venvs; set to a
## bare "uvicorn" to use whatever is on PATH (e.g. a system or conda env).
# PIPER_UVICORN=envs/piper/bin/uvicorn
# VAD_UVICORN=envs/vad/bin/uvicorn

## Default Piper voice (overridable per-request and via runtime.json).
# PIPER_DEFAULT_VOICE=en_US-lessac-medium

## How bin/warble manages Ollama:
##   external, you run Ollama yourself (or in Docker); warble only health-checks it. (default)
##   serve, warble runs `ollama serve` as a child process.
##   brew, macOS Homebrew: warble drives `brew services start/stop ollama`.
# OLLAMA_MODE=external
## Ollama log path (used by the "serve" and "brew" modes).
# OLLAMA_LOG=log/ollama.log

# Optional Ollama web search; export so the server inherits the key.
# export OLLAMA_API_KEY=your-key-here
